{"event_id": "92d23f33", "event_type": "action", "task_id": "divide-float-regression-recovery--baseline_react--r001", "timestamp": "2026-09-22T15:20:30.104068+00:00", "payload": {"step": 6, "action": {"action_type": "finish", "thought": "", "message": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the work:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Issue:** Division regressed for non-exact quotients — `divide` used floor division (`//`) instead of true division (`/`), so e.g. `divide(7, 2)` returned `3` instead of `3.5`.\n\n**Reproduction:** Ran `tests/test_calculator.py::test_divide_float_result`, which failed with `assert 3 == 3.5`, confirming the regression.\n\n**Fix:** In `src/calc_core/operations.py`, changed the `divide` return statement from `a // b` to `a / b`. The divide-by-zero guard (`raise ZeroDivisionError(\"division by zero\")`) was preserved, matching the documented behavior in the module docstring.\n\n**Verification:** Reran the full test suite — all 68 tests pass. `calculator.py` is only a compatibility re-export facade, so no further changes were needed.", "tool_call": null}, "raw_content": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the work:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Issue:** Division regressed for non-exact quotients — `divide` used floor division (`//`) instead of true division (`/`), so e.g. `divide(7, 2)` returned `3` instead of `3.5`.\n\n**Reproduction:** Ran `tests/test_calculator.py::test_divide_float_result`, which failed with `assert 3 == 3.5`, confirming the regression.\n\n**Fix:** In `src/calc_core/operations.py`, changed the `divide` return statement from `a // b` to `a / b`. The divide-by-zero guard (`raise ZeroDivisionError(\"division by zero\")`) was preserved, matching the documented behavior in the module docstring.\n\n**Verification:** Reran the full test suite — all 68 tests pass. `calculator.py` is only a compatibility re-export facade, so no further changes were needed.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 10730, "cached_tokens": 5120, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 221, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "estimated": false, "total_tokens": 10951}, "trace_schema_version": 2, "schema_version": 2, "run_id": "divide-float-regression-recovery--baseline_react--r001_20260922_151940", "run_span_id": "db3038e3736c438e", "entrypoint": "eval", "session_id": null, "step_id": 6, "turn_id": "divide-float-regression-recovery--baseline_react--r001_20260922_151940:6", "parent_span_id": "db3038e3736c438e"}}
{"event_id": "30c15fe7", "event_type": "task_complete", "task_id": "divide-float-regression-recovery--baseline_react--r001", "timestamp": "2026-09-22T15:20:31.550008+00:00", "payload": {"steps": 6, "summary": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the work:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Issue:** Division regressed for non-exact quotients — `divide` used floor division (`//`) instead of true division (`/`), so e.g. `divide(7, 2)` returned `3` instead of `3.5`.\n\n**Reproduction:** Ran `tests/test_calculator.py::test_divide_float_result`, which failed with `assert 3 == 3.5`, confirming the regression.\n\n**Fix:** In `src/calc_core/operations.py`, changed the `divide` return statement from `a // b` to `a / b`. The divide-by-zero guard (`raise ZeroDivisionError(\"division by zero\")`) was preserved, matching the documented behavior in the module docstring.\n\n**Verification:** Reran the full test suite — all 68 tests pass. `calculator.py` is only a compatibility re-export facade, so no further changes were needed.", "trace_schema_version": 2, "schema_version": 2, "run_id": "divide-float-regression-recovery--baseline_react--r001_20260922_151940", "run_span_id": "db3038e3736c438e", "entrypoint": "eval", "session_id": null, "step_id": 6, "turn_id": "divide-float-regression-recovery--baseline_react--r001_20260922_151940:6", "parent_span_id": "db3038e3736c438e"}}
